#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:18
msgid ""
"Parameters in ROS configure node behavior without requiring changes to the "
"node's source code. This article explains how parameters are structured, "
"declared, typed, updated, and monitored, helping you understand how to "
"manage configuration across a ROS system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:33
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr "目录"

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:36
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:38
msgid ""
"Parameters are configuration values stored by each node in the ROS graph. "
"Parameters are used to configure nodes at startup and during runtime, "
"without changing the code. You can set and change parameters using launch "
"files, command-line arguments, YAML files, the ``ros2 param`` command, and "
"the client library APIs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:43
msgid "Parameters in ROS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:45
msgid ""
"Parameters in ROS are associated with individual nodes. The lifetime of a "
"parameter is tied to the lifetime of the node (though the node could "
"implement some sort of persistence to reload values after restart)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:48
msgid ""
"Parameters are addressed by node name, node namespace, parameter name, and "
"parameter namespace. Providing a parameter namespace is optional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:51
msgid "Each parameter consists of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:53
msgid "Key: A string which is the parameter name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:55
msgid ""
"Value: The value of the parameter. One of the following types: ``bool``, "
"``int64``, ``float64``, ``string``, ``byte[]``, ``bool[]``, ``int64[]``, "
"``float64[]`` or ``string[]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:58
msgid ""
"Descriptor: An optional ``rcl_interfaces/msg/ParameterDescriptor`` that "
"describes the parameter and its constraints, such as a text description, "
"value ranges, type information, or making it read-only. By default, all "
"descriptors are empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:61
msgid ""
"For example, every node has a ``use_sim_time`` parameter with a boolean "
"value. It defaults to ``false``, but can be set to ``true`` when running in "
"simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:65
msgid "Setting and changing parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:67
msgid "In ROS, you can use multiple methods to set and change parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:69
msgid "At startup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:70
msgid ""
"Initial parameter values can be set when launching nodes through the ROS "
"launch facility. For more information about launch, see :doc:`../Developer-"
"Tools/Launch/Launch-Main`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:73
msgid ""
"Initial parameter values can also be set when running a node, either through "
"individual command-line arguments or through YAML files. "
"See :ref:`NodeArgsParameters`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:76
msgid "At runtime"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:77
msgid ""
"For nodes that are already running, the ``ros2 param`` command is the "
"primary way to interact with parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:79
msgid ""
"All client libraries also provide APIs to get, set, and react to parameter "
"changes while a node is running. The following client libraries are core to "
"ROS:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:82
msgid ""
"`rclcpp <https://index.ros.org/p/rclcpp/>`_: The C++ client library for ROS. "
"To learn more, see :doc:`client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/"
"Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-CPP` and :doc:`parameters/Working-with-"
"parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:85
msgid ""
"`rclpy <https://index.ros.org/p/rclpy/>`_: The Python client library for "
"ROS. To learn more, see :doc:`client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/"
"Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-Python` and :doc:`parameters/Working-with-"
"parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-Python`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:88
msgid ""
"To learn more about working with parameters, see :doc:`parameters/Working-"
"with-parameters`. For a hands-on tutorial with ROS parameters "
"see :doc:`parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/"
"Understanding-ROS2-Parameters`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:92
msgid "Parameter callbacks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:94
msgid ""
"A ROS node can optionally register three different types of callbacks to be "
"informed when changes are happening to parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:96
msgid ""
"Pre-set parameter callback: When it is called, it can modify the "
"``Parameter`` list to change, add, or remove entries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:97
msgid ""
"Set parameter callback: This callback gives you the ability to inspect the "
"upcoming change to the parameter and explicitly reject the change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:98
msgid ""
"Post-set parameter callback: This callback gives you the ability to react to "
"changes from parameters that have successfully been accepted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:100
msgid ""
"To learn how to register these callbacks, see :doc:`parameters/Working-with-"
"parameters`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:103
msgid "Migrating from ROS 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:105
msgid ""
"The :doc:`Launch file migration guide <../Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-"
"from-ROS1/Migrating-Launch-Files>` explains how to migrate ``param`` and "
"``rosparam`` launch tags from ROS 1 to ROS 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:107
msgid ""
"The :doc:`Migration guide <../Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/"
"Migrating-Parameters>` explains how to migrate parameters from ROS 1 to ROS "
"2."
msgstr ""

