#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:117
msgid "FAQs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:119
msgid "What does a parameter consist of?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:120
msgid ""
"Each parameter has a key, a value, and an optional descriptor. The key is "
"the parameter name, the value holds the data, and the descriptor can "
"describe constraints such as making the parameter read-only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:123
msgid "What types can a parameter value have?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:124
msgid ""
"A parameter value must be one of the following types: ``bool``, ``int64``, "
"``float64``, ``string``, ``byte[]``, ``bool[]``, ``int64[]``, ``float64[]``, "
"or ``string[]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:126
msgid "How can I set or change parameters?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:127
msgid ""
"You can set initial values at startup through the ROS launch facility, or "
"when you run a node with command-line arguments or YAML files. For nodes "
"that are already running, use the ``ros2 param`` command or the client "
"library APIs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:130
msgid "Can I change parameters while a node is running?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:131
msgid ""
"Yes. Use ``ros2 param`` from the command line, or use the get, set, and "
"reaction APIs in ``rclcpp`` or ``rclpy``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:134
msgid "What are parameter callbacks for?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Parameters.rst:135
msgid ""
"Parameter callbacks let a node respond when parameter changes are requested "
"or accepted. For example, the set parameter callback can inspect an upcoming "
"change and reject it."
msgstr ""
